Check the frozen Lean specification against one compiled ARM64 program. The driver
imports Machine, which defines machineSum and machineBound, and Spec, which defines
Sensitivity. Neither file can be changed. Choose one result.

PROVE followed by Lean declarations that include
theorem candidate : Sensitivity machineSum machineBound := ...
REFUTE followed by Lean declarations that include
theorem candidate : ¬ Sensitivity machineSum machineBound := ...
UNKNOWN if you cannot produce either proof.

The checker uses Lean 4.34.0 with the imports shown above and no Mathlib.
Use theorem for every proof declaration, including helpers. The lemma keyword
and the fin_cases tactic are unavailable. When using List.mem_finRange, pass the
index explicitly. The following helper shows the exact core Lean syntax.

theorem finiteCaseExample (i : Fin 5) (p : Fin 5 → Bool)
    (h : (List.finRange 5).all p = true) : p i = true :=
  (List.all_eq_true.mp h) i (List.mem_finRange i)

{replay_instructions}

Return the verdict on line one and only Lean declarations below it. Use def for
definitions and theorem for all proofs. Before submitting, check that you have
used theorem for every helper. Omit imports, set_option, comments, metaprogramming,
sorry, and native_decide.
